WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:03.400
Threat modeling requires knowing what needs protection.

00:00:03.620 --> 00:00:07.460
In an LLM system, assets are not limited to the model itself.

00:00:07.680 --> 00:00:13.200
The surrounding application, data, tools, outputs, and operational records can all matter.

00:00:13.420 --> 00:00:26.540
Assets may include user data, private documents, credentials, API keys, system prompts, business logic, model outputs, tool permissions, embeddings, logs, memory, and customer trust.

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:29.720
Some assets are sensitive because they are confidential.

00:00:29.940 --> 00:00:33.860
Others are sensitive because they influence decisions or actions.

00:00:34.080 --> 00:00:47.360
Security goals might include preventing data leakage, preserving output integrity, preventing unauthorized tool use, protecting secrets, limiting unsafe automation, maintaining auditability, and ensuring users understand when human review is needed.

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:50.460
The goal is not simply to make the model say safe things.

00:00:50.680 --> 00:00:55.880
The goal is to protect the system, users, data, and business process around the model.

00:00:56.100 --> 00:01:00.100
Clear assets and goals help the team choose controls that match real risk.
